{"ld": 901, "paper": "SP390", "session": "132", "title": "Resolve, Directing the Maine Redevelopment Land Bank Authority to Take Appropriate Actions to Identify Opportunities for the Beneficial Reuse of the Buildings and Land Commonly Known as the Bangor Mall (TITLE CHANGE)", "sponsor_id": "s-baldacci-joseph", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-rana-ambureen", "h-roeder-amy", "h-supica-laura"], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This resolve requires the Maine State Housing Authority to enter into negotiations to purchase the land and buildings located in the City of Bangor commonly known as the Bangor Mall. If, within 12 months of the effective date of this resolve, a purchase and sale agreement, or other contract for the purchase of the Bangor Mall has not been executed by 3204 all necessary parties, the Maine State Housing Authority is required to exercise its right of 3215 eminent domain to acquire the Bangor Mall. Within 6 months of acquiring the Bangor 3226 Mall, the Maine State Housing Authority is required to submit a report to the joint standing 3237 committee of the Legislature having jurisdiction over housing matters detailing the costs 3248 of converting the Bangor Mall into affordable housing units and proposing legislation to 3259 create the Bangor Mall Housing Authority. The area of operation of the Bangor Mall Housing Authority must be limited to the area of property conveyed to or taken by the Maine State Housing Authority under this resolve, and the area of operation of any municipal housing authority in the City of Bangor excludes this area. The resolve appropriates $25,000,000 to the Maine State Housing Authority for the purchase and 4304 improvement of the Bangor Mall.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0390&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Finally Passed", "final_disposition": {"label": "Finally Passed",